<title>CHINA: Shanghai interbank yuan market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Shanghai interbank yuan market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai's interbank yuan market was closed on Monday because of a National Day holiday, an exchange official said. Trading will resume on Thursday.</p>
<p>On Saturday, the last trading day, the China Interbank Offered Rate (CHIBOR), issued by the official Xinhua news agency on behalf of the People's Bank of China, the central bank, was as follows.</p>
<p>The figures represent weighted averages and not closing prices and are annual percentage rates.</p>
<p>The central bank does not post volumes.</p>
<p>		 1DAY    7DAY   20DAY  30DAY 60DAY   90DAY   120DAY</p>
<p>SATURDAY  no trade 11.340 11.160 12.960 11.700 12.240  no trade  FRIDAY     11.160  11.125 11.718 11.639 11.751 11.767  no trade</p>
</text>
